- Calling a field like `(hooks.allocate)(size)` needs the parentheses in Rust, because a field access followed by a call is parsed as a method call otherwise.
- The raw pointers keep the allocator interface faithful to the C code. Dereferencing a returned pointer is `unsafe`, but the calls themselves are safe.
